The code statements that lead to the bug are:

```c
tmp = (ichdr->count - 1) * sizeof(xfs_attr_leaf_entry_t) + xfs_attr3_leaf_hdr_size(leaf);
if (ichdr->freemap[i].base == tmp) {
    ichdr->freemap[i].base += sizeof(xfs_attr_leaf_entry_t);
    ichdr->freemap[i].size -= min_t(uint16_t, ichdr->freemap[i].size, sizeof(xfs_attr_leaf_entry_t));
}
```

Reason:
The old code only adjusts a freemap entry if its `base` exactly equals the old end of the leaf entry array (`tmp`). If a freemap entry starts anywhere between the old end and the new end (i.e., within the space the new entry will occupy), it is left unchanged. This causes the freemap to claim free space that is actually now part of the entry array, resulting in overlapping free space claims. The inconsistency later triggers the assertion `ASSERT(ichdr->firstused >= ichdr->count * sizeof(xfs_attr_leaf_entry_t) + xfs_attr3_leaf_hdr_size(leaf))` because `firstused` falls below the end of the entry array.

The code statements that fix the bug are:

```c
new_end = ichdr->count * sizeof(struct xfs_attr_leaf_entry) + xfs_attr3_leaf_hdr_size(leaf);
old_end = new_end - sizeof(struct xfs_attr_leaf_entry);
for (i = 0; i < XFS_ATTR_LEAF_MAPSIZE; i++) {
    int diff = 0;
    if (ichdr->freemap[i].base == old_end) {
        diff = sizeof(struct xfs_attr_leaf_entry);
    } else if (ichdr->freemap[i].size > 0 && ichdr->freemap[i].base < new_end) {
        diff = new_end - ichdr->freemap[i].base;
    }
    if (diff) {
        ichdr->freemap[i].base += diff;
        ichdr->freemap[i].size -= min_t(uint16_t, ichdr->freemap[i].size, diff);
    }
}
```

Reason:
The fix first computes the old and new ends of the leaf entry array. For each freemap entry, it now checks two cases: if the entry starts exactly at the old end, it is shifted by the size of one leaf entry; or if the entry starts before the new end (i.e., it lies within the space that the new entry will occupy), it is shifted by the full amount needed to push its base beyond the new end. This ensures that no freemap entry overlaps with the expanded entry array, eliminating the inconsistent free space claims and preventing the assertion failure. The patch also resets zero‑length freemap entries to avoid later confusion.

